        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-27T21:18:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is impossible to do that on the alloc and free paths when the lock is in the structure you are allocating and freeing. I think it is better to put a comment here than acquiring a lock that can\u0027t safely be held by any other thread. I don\u0027t think the linux mutex_unlock guarantees that mutex_unlock has stopped accessing any part of the lock struct before releasing the lock.",
